# Production secret files

Create these files with mode `0600`, owned by the deployment operator. Each
file contains only the secret value and one optional trailing newline.

- `postgres_password`
- `database_password`
- `redis_password`
- `jwt_secret` (at least 32 random characters)
- `storage_access_key_id`
- `storage_secret_access_key`
- `backup_age_recipient` (public `age1...` recipient)
- `backup_age_identity` (private AGE-SECRET-KEY file; restore tooling only)
- `backup_signing_private_key` (passwordless minisign key, backup writer only)
- `backup_signing_public_key` (minisign public verification key)
- `backup_s3_access_key_id`
- `backup_s3_secret_access_key`
- `tls.crt` (full certificate chain)
- `tls.key` (private TLS key)

Optional integrations use `ai_api_key`, `stripe_secret_key`,
`stripe_webhook_secret`, and `smtp_password`. Grant each Compose service only
the files it consumes.
